<title>USA: INTERVIEW -- CUC Intl, HFS Inc.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW -- CUC Intl, HFS Inc.</headline>
<byline>Brendan Intindola</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The $11 billion stock-swap merger of CUC International Inc and HFS Inc will raise CUC's estimated earnings to as high as $1.23 per share in the fiscal year ending January 1998, up from an analysts' range of $0.88 to $1.10 per share, CUC's chairman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Wall Street has us at $0.88 or $0.89 to $1.10 next year. With this acquisition it looks like $0.97 to $1.23, plus or minus a few cents,&quot; chairman Walter Forbes told Reuters in an interview.</p>
</text>
